{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>As HaShem commanded Moses.</b> The reason Scripture says so for every single detail is according to what we wrote in parashat Tetzaveh (Exodus 27:20), that HaShem apportioned to Moses a share in every labor and service performed in the Mishkan, for his share in the deed is the commandment that HaShem commands the matter through him. Therefore it mentions him for every single detail — that even though he does not perform it himself, he is nevertheless the one commanding that it be done." "<b>Further,</b> it intends that at the time of the work they would say: ״Behold, we are doing this thing <b>as HaShem commanded Moses</b>.״" "<b>Further,</b> it appears according to what has preceded us, that there is no commandment that does not contain details of intellectual insight, and only a fraction was written in the Torah, as Rabbi Yohanan's statement in ha-Nizzakin (Gittin 60b); and besides this, every single deed of the Mishkan contains an intelligible dimension, which is the inner core of the things. And these are to be performed with intention of the heart and in the hidden intellection, and a thing is performed through its own kind, as is known to those who possess knowledge and understanding, and this is what the Torah alluded to in every detail — <b>as HaShem commanded Moses</b> — meaning, orally, and it is not spelled out in the Torah on account of the preciousness of the matter. And I will grant you insight: that what is written is from the perspective of the effect (מופעל), while the intelligible (מושכל) is abstracted from receiving some of it in the perspective of the agent (מפעיל), and some of it also from the perspective of the speaker (מדבר), for it is far removed in two degrees. And some of what HaShem alluded to is in the effect (נפעל), seen yet not seen, in the sod of the form of the letters and their cantillation signs and the crowns upon their heads — the tagin — and their deeds, which are called the dimension of thought, and wonders beyond wonders were revealed to Moses at Sinai. Go and learn from the derashah of Rabbi Akiva (Sanhedrin 106a) — three hundred halakhot in the crown of the lamed; these saw the deeds of HaShem. And Scripture informs us for all the details of the Mishkan that they made it <b>as HaShem commanded Moses</b> — according to all the wonders that were intended upon them."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {2 "The philosophical terms מופעל/מפעיל/נפעל/מושכל and מדבר are rendered literally as effect/agent/effect(passive)/intelligible and speaker; their precise technical interrelation in this passage is deliberately left opaque as in the source."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:37:19.376698374Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}